.TH tucolumn 1 0.29.0 tclutils "Tcl Utility Command"
.SH NAME
tucolumn \- thin CLI wrapper for tclutils::tucolumn
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
tucolumn ?table|fill? ?-separator S? ?-output S? ?-right 0|1? ?-width N? ?-gap N? ?file?
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The tucolumn command is a thin wrapper around the Tcl package tclutils::tucolumn. It is intended for interactive and scripting use when tclutils is installed from source. The primary API remains the Tcl library; see tucolumn(n) for procedures, options, and semantics.
.PP
Run the script with tclsh:
.PP
.nf
tclsh bin/tucolumn.tcl ...
.fi
